# UITK BEM transition standard (ADR 039)

Authority: [UITK BEM transition guide](../docs/04-dev/uitk-bem-transition-guide.md) (API + recipes), [ADR 039](../decisions/039-uitk-dotween-show-hide.md) §3 + §6, [centralized-ui-gotchas](../docs/04-dev/centralized-ui-gotchas.md) (symptoms).

## Transition helpers (`*Transition.cs`)

- Steady visibility lives in **BEM modifiers**; motion uses **inline `style`** during tweens only.
- **`onComplete` / `Reset`:** call `BemMotionCompletion.ApplySteadyClassThenClearMotion(target, steadyClass, active)` — never `ClearMotionStyles` before the steady class.
- Collapse with `pickingMode`: use `CollapseTransition`’s `ApplyCollapsedSteady` (wraps class + picking + clear).
- Add **two** Edit Mode tests in `UiToolkitTweensTests`: present clears steady hidden class; dismiss sets steady hidden class.

## Presenter sync (`SyncPresentation`, chrome visibility)

- Gate on **steady hidden class** on the animation target + `IsSettling` via `VisualPresentationSync.ShouldCallShow` / `ShouldCallHide`.
- Do **not** skip `Show()` only because `IsShown` is true — retracted/faded class may be off mid-dismiss tween.
- Prefer deriving public `IsShown` from steady class when the animation target is the surface (`MapView`, `CommandRailInfoPresenter`).
- One phase owner per chrome; avoid duplicate visibility apply in the same frame.

## No hard cuts

- **Player-visible dismiss** → `Hide()` / facade `Clear` + presentation driver (slide/fade/pop-in). Not `HideImmediate()` while chrome is on screen or dismiss is settling.
- **`HideImmediate()`** → `OnDisable`, shared-picker **context enum swap**, competing overlay handoff, chrome already steady-hidden. Not mid-beat snap from Runtime (`FloorTransitionPresenter`, gates) while phase fade is in progress.
- **One owner per beat** — phase host clears at transition **start**; cross-system code uses `Hide()` or skips if owner already cleared. Republish on `PresentationReleased`.
- **No dual authority** — do not stack USS `display: none` on parent with slide/fade on child in `SyncPresentation` else branches.
- Full policy: [UITK BEM transition guide § No hard cuts](https://github.com/miramocha/griddungeon-design-docs/blob/main/docs/04-dev/uitk-bem-transition-guide.md#no-hard-cuts-player-visible-showhide).

## Exceptions (do not force this pattern)

| Area | Why |
|------|-----|
| PopIn pickers | Host `tabbed-picker--hidden`; race is `Refresh` vs `Show` during settle |
| `MapViewPanelTransition` | Layout dimensions, not show/hide authority |
| `ScreenFadePresenter` | Imperative full-screen fade |

## PR checklist

- [ ] ADR 039 §3 row for new steady class
- [ ] `BemMotionCompletion` or documented exception
- [ ] `VisualPresentationSync` or visual `IsShown`
- [ ] `UiToolkitTweensTests` + presenter settle test if behavior changed
- [ ] No player-visible hard cut — `Hide`/`Clear` at beat start; `HideImmediate` only per guide § No hard cuts
